Upstream data and software

This repository contains study code and processed analysis files. It does
not bundle raw sequencing reads, original CTSS resources, reference genomes
or third-party software source distributions.

ENCODE: source files are identified in DATA.md. ENCODE permits unrestricted
use of released data; please credit the producing labs and the project.
https://www.encodeproject.org/about/data-use-policy/

FANTOM5: FANTOM5 © RIKEN licensed under CC Attribution 4.0 International.
The study derives promoter-group support labels from FANTOM5 CTSS data;
those labels are not the original CTSS files.
https://fantom.gsc.riken.go.jp/
https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/fantom5/lic.html

LRGASP and GEO: obtain the candidate submissions and GSE185917 source files
from their providers. Their identifiers and processing roles are listed in
DATA.md. Cite the original resource when reusing these inputs:
Pardo-Palacios et al. Nature Methods (2024).
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-024-02298-3
https://lrgasp.github.io/lrgasp-submissions/
https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/query/acc.cgi?acc=GSE185917

Software dependencies keep their own licenses. Installing a package listed
in requirements.txt does not transfer that package's copyright or license
to this project. In particular, the included study adapters are not copies
of the full PSQAN or SQANTI3 software distributions.

The repository licenses cover only the rights held by the study authors.
They do not supersede upstream terms or claim ownership of public source
data. Check the original providers for the terms applicable to their files.
